research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl-51-{"id":"thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"Verified all four claims (a)-(d) against their cited facts: step 1.1 correctly uses [L1],[L2],[L4] to show naturals are cardinals; step 1.2 correctly uses [L1] to show omega is a cardinal; step 1.3 correctly constructs the shift bijection kappa->beta using [L4],[L8],[L9] to prove infinite cardinals are limit ordinals; step 2.1 correctly uses [L1],[L2],[L4],[L5],[L6] to identify finite and cardinal |A|; steps 1.4 and 3.1 correctly use [L6],[L7],[L9],[L10] to establish the arithmetic dictionary. All [L#] facts faithfully restate their cited items, the title matches what is proved, and no choice principle is used.","at":"2026-07-28T18:48:10.652Z"}
research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl-52-{"id":"ex-the-diagonal-of-the-real-line-is-closed","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the proof step by step: A1-A3 and L1 faithfully restate their cited sources, the triangle inequality argument in step 3.1 correctly derives a contradiction, and step 4.1 correctly applies the closure characterization to conclude the diagonal is closed. The implicit use of A ⊆ closure(A) in step 4.1 is part of claim 2 of the cited theorem and is closeable in seconds. Title matches what is proved.","at":"2026-07-28T18:48:11.347Z"}
research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl-53-{"id":"def-connected-component-and-quasicomponent","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the definition's well-posedness: C(x) is correctly shown connected via thm-unions-of-connected-sets claim 1 (family nonempty by singleton connectedness from def-connected-space, common point x), and largest containing x; Q(x) family nonempty via X clopen from def-topological-space; totally disconnected equivalence, empty space case, and discrete space argument are all correct with faithful citations.","at":"2026-07-28T18:48:30.156Z"}
research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl-54-{"id":"thm-compactness-under-continuous-maps","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"Verified all three claims: claim 1 (steps 1.1–5.1) correctly constructs preimage covers, applies compactness, recovers finitely many U_j via finite choice, and extends to compact subsets via restriction; claim 2 (steps 5.2–7.1) correctly proves max/min by contradiction using open ray covers and [L7]–[L8]; claim 3 (steps 6.2, 8.1) correctly shows f is a closed map via [L9]–[L10] and concludes via [L11]. Every [L#] fact faithfully restates its cited source, and every proof step is licensed by the facts it cites.","at":"2026-07-28T18:48:41.499Z"}
research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl-55-{"id":"ex-the-diagonal-in-the-cofinite-and-cocountable-topologies","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"Verified all proof steps against their cited facts: step 1.1 correctly uses A1/A3/L1 for T1 via closed singletons; step 1.2 correctly proves non-disjointness of nonempty cofinite opens via De Morgan and infinitude of X; step 1.3 correctly cites L4 which faithfully restates fs-unique-sequential-limits-imply-hausdorff; step 1.5 correctly derives discreteness of cocountable on countable Z via L5; steps 2.1-3.1 correctly use L2 (closure characterization) to show closure of diagonal equals the whole square, then L3 to conclude non-Hausdorff; step 4.1 correctly concludes the countable case is discrete hence Hausdorff with closed diagonal. Title matches what is proved. No mis-citations, logical gaps, or contradictions with siblings or companion page found.","at":"2026-07-28T18:48:58.660Z"}
research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl-56-{"id":"lem-the-partial-alternating-sum-of-a-binomial-row","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the induction proof on m for fixed t>=1: base case m=0 gives both sides equal to 1 via L2, L4, L5; inductive step correctly applies Pascal's rule (L3) at n=s, k=m with s+1=t to expand binom(t,m+1), uses additivity of iota (L4) to split, extends the sum by one term via the recursion clause (L2), and simplifies using (-1)^{m+1}=-(-1)^m (L5) and field algebra to obtain (-1)^{m+1} iota binom(s,m+1). All [L#] facts faithfully restate their cited items. The t>=1 hypothesis is correctly located at s+1=t, and the counterexample at t=0, m=1 is accurately described.","at":"2026-07-28T18:49:18.009Z"}
research/frontier-2-judge.jsonl-57-{"id":"lem-tube-lemma-for-a-compact-factor","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the tube lemma proof step by step: [L1] faithfully restates the product topology basis for a binary product, [L2] faithfully restates the basis property from def-topology-basis-subbasis, [L3] faithfully restates claim 2 of lem-compactness-of-a-subspace-is-ambient, and [L4] faithfully restates the topology axioms. The cover is correctly indexed by pairs (U,V) so compactness returns indices carrying their own V components, the empty-K case is handled, W is a well-defined finite intersection of open sets containing z0, and the final inclusion K×W⊆N follows correctly from the finite subcover and the definition of P. No choice principle is used, no citation is misstated, and no logical gap exists.","at":"2026-07-28T18:49:27.961Z"}
